# Backend Architecture

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/backend.md`, `docs/architecture/workspace-topology.md`.

## Layers (dependency points inward)

```
apps/api, apps/worker          ← thin transport (LoggerLocator.init; api also ApiBuilder)
  → nest-http                  ← HTTP kit (pipe/filter/Swagger/CORS/versioning)
  → composition/<context>      ← Nest modules (port → adapter wiring)
  → infrastructure/{postgres,logger,redis,messaging}
  → application/<context>      ← @Injectable use cases
  → domain/<context>           ← pure models + repository PORTS
  → shared-kernel-types

platform                       ← capability ports (Cache, Lock, PubSub, UnitOfWork, Logger locator)
```

Bounded contexts are **folders** inside each layer: `identity`, `tenancy`, `authorization`, `audit`, `notifications`.

## Apps (thin)

Controllers/processors only: validate with contracts via `nest-http`, map DTO → command, call use cases. No business logic, no TypeORM, no Redis. `apps/api` imports `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/nest-http` and `composition` — not `postgres` / `domain` / `application`. Bootstrap: `LoggerLocator.init(new PinoLogger(...))` then `ApiBuilder`. Routes are `/v1/...`.

```typescript
// apps/api — members controller
@Controller()
export class MembersController {
  constructor(private readonly members: MembersService) {}

  @RequirePermission('tenancy.members.read')
  @ApiRoute(MembersRoutes.list) // path: 'tenants/:tenantId/members'
  async list(@Param() {tenantId}: TenantIdParamDto) {
    return this.members.list(tenantId)
  }
}
```

## Application

- `@Injectable` use cases only Nest seam allowed
- Own transaction boundaries via `UnitOfWork`
- Own fine-grained authorization
- Depend on **ports** from `domain` / `platform`, never on infrastructure
- Log with `LoggerLocator.get().context(CreateUserUseCase.name)` — **never** `@Inject()` Logger
- Never import `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts`

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class InviteMemberUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly uow: UnitOfWork,
    private readonly authz: AuthorizationPort,
    private readonly memberships: MembershipRepository,
  ) {}

  async execute(cmd: InviteMemberCommand) {
    await this.authz.require(cmd.actorUserId, 'tenant.members.invite', {
      tenantId: cmd.tenantId,
    })
    return this.uow.run(async () => {
      const membership = Membership.invite(cmd)
      await this.memberships.save(membership)
      return membership
    })
  }
}
```

## Domain

Pure TypeScript. Repository **ports** live here. No Nest, TypeORM, Redis, or HTTP. See `domain-layer.mdc`.

## Platform

Capability ports only (`CachePort`, `LockPort`, `PubSubPort`, `UnitOfWork`, `Clock`, `IdGenerator`, `Logger`). `LoggerLocator` is a process locator, not Nest DI. Pino adapter lives in `packages/infrastructure/logger`.

## Infrastructure

Implements ports. TypeORM entities + mappers in `packages/infrastructure/postgres`. Pino in `packages/infrastructure/logger` (no Nest). Redis adapters in `packages/infrastructure/redis`. Never export entities outside this layer.

## nest-http

Delivery kit (`ApiBuilder`, global pipe/filter/interceptor, Swagger, CORS, URI versioning, `@Public()`). Not composition. Does not import domain/application/postgres.

## Composition

Per-context Nest modules bind ports → adapters and register use cases. Apps import composition modules.

```typescript
@Module({
  providers: [
    InviteMemberUseCase,
    { provide: MembershipRepository, useClass: TypeOrmMembershipRepository },
  ],
  exports: [InviteMemberUseCase],
})
export class TenancyModule {}
```

## Forbidden

- Domain/application importing infrastructure or Nest beyond `@Injectable`
- `@Inject()` Logger or `nestjs-pino`
- Application importing `contracts`
- Business logic in controllers
- Pipes/filters/Swagger copied into `apps/api` instead of `nest-http`
- Cross-context imports of domain internals (use IDs + events)
